From a6054c1e45fc6e843e0ef2cca9e12767c1cf170c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:23:56 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH] PCI/MSI: notify drivers of permanent interrupt delivery
 loss

Notify a driver when a controller has permanently blocked MSI delivery.
Serialize recovery against driver removal and system sleep, and report
whether the callback recovered service or left it unresolved.

Provide a separate software-only failure notification when recovery is
unavailable. Document binding changes, callback locking and return values;
neither notification establishes DMA completion or frees queue resources.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/PCI/index.rst             |   1 +
 Documentation/PCI/msi-delivery-loss.rst | 113 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/pci/msi/api.c                   |  91 +++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/pci.h                     |  32 +++++++
 4 files changed, 237 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/PCI/msi-delivery-loss.rst

